{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106630","id":2531172306,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6W3p_S","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106630","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106630.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106630.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106630","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106630/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106630/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106630/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/6504ca11f34a7296dc415cfd358794f5cd829da2","number":106630,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Fix finished signal on GPU particles","user":{"login":"miv391","id":49998025,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5OTk4MDI1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49998025?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391","html_url":"https://github.com/miv391","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/93991\r\n\r\nFixes two issues:\r\n1. `finished` signal is now emitted when continuously emitting `GPUParticles2D` (or 3D) is stopped by setting `one_shot` to true. \r\n    - Previously `finished` signal was not emitted and it was extremely difficult to work with particles. I have a lot of use cases where I need to do something when the particles are stopped.\r\n    - There was a workaround which at least sometimes worked. Calling `gpu_particles_2d.restart()` in `_ready()` function allowed `finished` signal to emit.\r\n\r\nSo this kind of code works now:\r\n```gdscript\r\nfunc _on_button_pressed() -> void:\r\n\tgpu_particles_2d.one_shot = true\r\n\tgpu_particles_2d.finished.connect(func(): prints(\"FINISHED!!!!!\"))\r\n```\r\n\r\n2. Setting `one_shot` to `false` when it already is `false` no longer resets the particle system. \r\n\r\nI tested master's CPUParticles2D and that doesn't have same problem.","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":4442850752,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCNCFwA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:particles","name":"topic:particles","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release.","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.